<%#
  Deliberately skipping widget_wrapper here (which would add its own
  Primer title-bar box) -- the Angular side (pmo-dashboard-widget.component)
  already renders a simple header, and the card partial below has its own
  colored project-name header. Two header layers would be one too many.

  The turbo-frame wrapper is still required though: Turbo only swaps in a
  fetched response if it contains a <turbo-frame> whose id matches the
  requesting frame (grids-widgets-pmo-dashboard, set on the Angular side)
  -- widget_wrapper would normally provide that for free.

  No _styles partial anymore -- the redesigned card (see _card.html.erb)
  uses inline styles throughout, not the old .pmo-* CSS classes.
%>
<%= helpers.turbo_frame_tag "grids-widgets-pmo-dashboard" do %>
  <%= render partial: "pmo_dashboard/card", locals: { summary: summary } %>
<% end %>
